                <pb facs="0517" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 9160/58.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Chargé
                    Sands.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic">December 7,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bacon informs Mr. Sands that the Government of Guatemala has requested
                    further time to investigate facts in the cases of Shine and Milliken, and
                    directs that he informally advise the minister of foreign affairs that the
                    United States Government is prepared to allow ample time for a thorough
                    investigation of the facts of these cases. Instructs Mr. Sands to continue his
                    investigations, reporting all material facts to department, and to take no
                    further action in the matter until further instructed by department.</p>
            </div>
